From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:06:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deploy): pass the Databricks feature list by environment

deploy.py handed the --features list to the bundle as
`--var features=<list>`. The Databricks CLI splits --var values on
commas, so the documented comma-separated usage failed as soon as a
deploy named more than one feature:

    Error: unexpected flag value for variable assignment: automations_v2

The bind, deploy and run commands now go through one helper that gives
the child process BUNDLE_VAR_features, which the CLI takes verbatim, and
the --var pair is gone. The deploy's own environment is not changed.

Not checked against a live workspace here; the environment form was used
for multi-feature deploys with Databricks CLI v1.26.0 before this
rewrite (https://github.com/Desidero/omnigent/issues/20).

Not upstream yet: not proposed, and there is no contribution branch for
it; drop this copy once upstream fixes the same bug.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (fix: the documented --features list now deploys; deploy/databricks/README.md notes the variable for manual bundle runs)
